    <statement><p>Let <m>z=g(u,v,w,x)</m> and
<m>u(r,s,t),v(r,s,t),w(r,s,t),x(r,s,t)</m>.
How many terms are there in the expression for <m>\partial z/\partial r</m>?</p>
<p><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/> terms</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t} =
    g_{u}\cdot u_{r}+g_{v}\cdot v_{r}+g_{w}\cdot w_{r}+g_{x}\cdot x_{r}.</me>
Thus, there are 4 terms.




</solution>
